6. HIGH-STAKES STATE: NO ANCHOR RENDERS UNKNOWN, NEVER $0.00 -- PASS
Verified in RENDERED MARKUP, not handler state. A checking account with no
anchors, served from the real binary, produced this card row:

  "No Anchor Checking &middot; Local CU Data through Aug 13, 2026
   Balance unknown  Set an anchor on the accounts page
   No balance anchor set &mdash; the balance is unknown, not zero.
   Projection unavailable &mdash; no balance anchor set."

Programmatic check on that <li>: contains "$0.00"? False. Contains ANY `\$\d`?
False. The row carries no dollar figure at all. TestAccountsCard_NoAnchor pins
this, correctly scoping the assertion to extractAccountsCardSection so the KPI
tiles' legitimate $0.00 cannot mask a regression.

7. ALL FOUR CARD STATES RENDER DISTINCTLY -- PASS
One fixture with four accounts, read out of the served dashboard:
  low       Chase Everyday  $235.80  + "Below the $500 low-balance threshold" + icon
  no-anchor Vanguard        "Balance unknown" (no figure) + "unknown, not zero" + icon
  stale     Ally Savings    $7,512.50 + "Data is stale -- the balance may not
                            reflect recent activity. Re-import the CSV..." + icon
  healthy   USAA Checking   $8,412.66, no flag, no icon
A stale CSV cannot look healthy: Ally shows a balance AND an explicit staleness
sentence. Precedence in accounts_card.go is no-anchor > stale > low > healthy,
so a stale-and-low account reports stale (the balance itself may be wrong) --
sound judgment call, documented at the code site.

8. LOW AND STALE ARE NOT COLOR-ONLY (ACCESSIBILITY.md point 8) -- PASS
Each flag div contains an `<svg aria-hidden="true">` AND a `<span>` of literal
text. Counted in served HTML: low/stale/no-anchor rows carry 1 icon each;
healthy carries 0 (correctly, it has no flag). Meaning survives with color
removed.

9. PROJECTION LINE, ALL THREE STATES -- PASS
  crossing     "Drops below $500 around Aug 14, 2026 -- no prior transfers to
                reference. Suggested top-up: $300."
  no-crossing  "Projected to stay above the $500 threshold for the next 35 days."
  unavailable  "Projection unavailable -- no balance anchor set."
All three observed in served markup (unavailable required a checking account
with no anchor, since brokerage kinds get no projection line at all -- correct
per spec, which scopes the line to checking/savings). accounts_card.go calls
accounts.Project / BalanceAt / Freshness directly and adds no arithmetic of its
own; the only new number is the presentation-layer staleAccountDays=45
threshold, which is a UI concern and documented as such.

